WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.601
You have the mercenaries.

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.302
Mercenary groups

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.704
like Wagner, with Yevgeny Prigozhin

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.539
looking over Putin's shoulder,

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.874
getting ever more powerful,

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.443
make him more money out of this war.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.612
And that also is a kind of a threat

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.214
for Putin to people

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.616
other than him with getting more power.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.385
All right, Nick, thank you very much.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:20.487
Live from Kramatorsk.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.623
OUTFRONT now, Boris Bond.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.791
He was a Russian diplomat

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:25.592
for 20 years

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:26.826
and resigned in protest

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.062
over Putin's war in Ukraine.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.830
Boris I appreciate your time tonight.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.767
One person we've spoken a lot about

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.368
on this show

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.671
who appears to be close to Putin now

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.874
seems to want to run this war

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.509
in a much bigger way of

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.277
is Evgeny Prigozhin,

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.578
the head of the volunteer group,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.881
paramilitary organization.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.116
Do you think promotion could take over?

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.385
What is his role with Putin?

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.889
Well, it's a very

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.891
interesting moment in all of this

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.093
campaign that Mr.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:03.196
Prigozhin has become so influential

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.432
and it really,

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.766
really is the person

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:10.070
which can decide a lot of, you know,

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.706
can make a lot of decisions

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.042
So I think he is

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.078
somehow a favorite

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.246
of sledging and Putin for now.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:20.914
And Vladimir

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.683
Putin obviously interests him

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.053
with the most difficult and challenging

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:30.090
missions on the frontline, because Mr.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.891
Prigozhin controls

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.828
these private military companies

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:37.530
like Vladimir is one of them.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.833
And they are known.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.767
They are notorious

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.036
for being the most effective

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:43.970
the most cruel

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.340
of all Russian armed structures

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.977
in which are acting now in Ukraine.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.780
But I believe that Mr.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.380
President has

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.182
no political future in Russia

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.418
because he has no social bases

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.353
and he has no allies

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.855
within the Russian establishment,

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:05.525
because all of the Russian establishment

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:09.062
I mean, decision makers, such as army

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:12.932
generals or special service people,

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.034
they hate him and despise him

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.202
as a former criminal

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.271
and someone who has no

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.472
connections because

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.877
you know jumped up man or something.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.378
So I would not

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.481
overestimate his significance for now.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.650
Do you read anything into this, though?

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:31.351
You don't want to

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.785
overestimate his significance,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.220
but does his rise

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.488
and the fact that you say

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.424
so many in power despise him?

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.527
What does this mean about Putin

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.494
that Putin is seems to

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.196
seems to be letting him in more?

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:45.532
Is it a sign of Putin's isolation?

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:46.199
Is it a sign

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:49.502
others are turning against Putin?

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.171
How do you see it?

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:53.706
Well,

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.876
I would like to see it as the sign

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.144
of a further isolation

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.612
of Putin, of course, because

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.381
and his frustration

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:04.017
that Putin is obviously disappointed

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:04.884
in his army,

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:08.221
his generals, which cannot deal brief,

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.923
you know, victory over Ukraine,

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.457
which they had promised

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:12.792
to him, obviously,

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.761
before the war started.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.529
And of course, he now

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.498
seems that maybe proportion with his,

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.465
you know,

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.468
unscrupulous methods of war can

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.438
have some victories. Who knows?

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:28.341
But of course, but any and any of this

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:31.978
will lead to further destabilization

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.513
within the Russian elite.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:35.782
It is obvious one way or another,

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.584
Putin will be more dependent

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:39.752
on Prigozhin and his like

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.020
or he will stay more

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.389
dependent on army generals and FSB

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.958
generals, for instance.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.726
And those two groups

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.461
will be in constant fight

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:50.163
with each other that maybe Mr.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:52.232
Putin is counting on this.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.468
So they are they fighting each other

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:59.272
and he can still be a part of this fight.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.741
But for how long? I don't know.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:03.376
At one point in

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.177
your career,

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.078
you worked for the Foreign

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.746
Minister Ministries Department

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.982
for Nonproliferation and Arms Control,

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.984
and that was obviously related

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:13.019
to weapons of mass destruction.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.354
The latest we have from U.S.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.022
intelligence is that senior Russian

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:16.923
military officials

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.391
have discussed specifics

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.492
how under

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.693
what conditions

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:21.294
to use

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:23.363
a tactical nuclear weapon in Ukraine.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.331
Do you think the possibility of this

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.500
is increasing at all

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:30.903
I believe

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.872
there is still the possibility

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.274
of using nuclear weapons

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.041
on the Russian side.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.342
And of course,

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.745
because, of course, every general

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:39.679
wants to use

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.581
whatever means he has in order

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.016
to gain a victory.

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:45.084
And Russian generals are no exceptions.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:48.254
And, of course, they see that they

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.390
they have no prospects

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.859
of winning this war or even,

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:54.427
you know,

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:54.794
to have

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:57.096
a kind of an acceptable stalemate

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.197
for Russia.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:01.434
And, of course, I think they naturally,

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.369
they're discussing the scenarios

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:06.806
of how they could deploy nuclear weapons

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.342
but they don't think well.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:12.645
I think even to me, as a non-specialist,

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:14.113
an expert in military

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.381
and military affairs,

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.383
you know, secret military affairs,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.651
it is obvious that

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.320
even if they use new tactical

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.020
nuclear weapons,

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.423
it will not change the course of the war

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.892
because it will have

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:28.428
very limited military gains

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.463
and it will have a devastating

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:33.032
political consequences for Russia.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.567
Our Boris, I appreciate your time.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:35.535
Thank you so much.

